@chris-morgan:
> I’ve already [made a patch](https://github.com/chris-morgan/html/tree/QUERY) because I was curious to go through and see where I reckoned modifications might be needed, but I submit this as an issue because the thing is unsolicited and I also doubt the patch is ready as-is—“POST resource” really wants a new name,

The spec change in #11347 handles the "POST resource" naming issue! If WHATWG were interested, I would be happy to refactor it out of my PR and merge it separately.

@samuel-ifrs:
> PUT/PATCH/DELETE are unsafe and raise real CORS/security questions for form submission.

As implemented in #11347, proposal #3577 does not raise any CORS concerns because PUT, PATCH, and DELETE methods are CORS-enabled by default; they're actually safer than the existing POST forms, which have [CORS exceptions](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Guides/CORS#simple_requests). If you have some other security concern in mind, though, please do call it out on the issue tracker.
